{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Implementation summary (three-layer prune safety)\n\nFull design/rollback: host-local doc `docs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md` (git-ignored). Fix is entirely in the host-local updater `~/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh` (not in this repo); backup at `.pre-df15`.\n\nLayer 1 — bounded retention: `RELEASES_KEEP=3`. Never prune current`s target nor the newest 3 by mtime.\nLayer 2 — flock liveness pinning: `~/.local/bin/{rebar,rebar-mcp}` are now wrapper shims that take a SHARED non-blocking flock on `<release>/.inuse`, held across `exec` via an inherited fd. The pruner takes an EXCLUSIVE non-blocking flock before deleting; refusal ⇒ live ⇒ keep.\nLayer 3 — cap + alert: `RELEASES_CAP=10`. If exceeded because live releases cannot be reclaimed, emit an SNS alert (topic `rebar-gerrit-alerts`, us-east-1 → joeoakhart@navapbc.com, throttled 1/24h) instead of deleting a live release or growing unbounded. Also alerts after 3 consecutive candidate rejections.\n\nVerification: offline oracles A/B/C/C-neg/D/E + defect-seeded mutation (data loss reproduced without fix, absent with it); by-hand run built origin/main 6e282021, installed shims, pruned safely; launchd re-enabled (`launchctl list` + kickstart exit 0); AC-2 live spanning test = 0 failures across 3 forced update cycles with a long-lived global rebar-mcp pinned throughout."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787241049336089001,"uuid":"ba676e65-ad3b-4870-88b9-1b6829a70ea3"}